cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Malek Symbiosis Standard, please cite it as below."
title: "Malek Symbiosis Standard (MSS)"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Małek"
    given-names: "Mateusz"
version: "4.5.0"
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
abstract: >-
  The Malek Symbiosis Standard (MSS) is a decision-discipline framework for
  work between a human and an AI: a fixed order of checks you put to a
  decision before you act on it, covering whether the consequence is
  reversible or irreversible, a framework gate of eight named principles with
  a binary verdict, a review of five questions answered in sentences, and a
  required statement of the limits of this assessment. It carries no scores, no
  percentages and no confidence values — every answer names the party it
  concerns, and the result is written down.
keywords:
  - decision making
  - human-AI collaboration
  - AI ethics
  - AI governance
  - accountability
  - irreversibility
  - applied ethics
  - decision framework
